@@ -152,6 +152,7 @@ Legend: `[x]` done in code · `[~]` partly done / needs your device to confirm 
 | 0150 | 2026-10-17 | Square history can be copied from one register to another by QR (your request). **Settings ▸ Square history ▸ Share with another register ▸ Show QR for another register** turns the register into what the PC script is: a small read-only web server on the shop Wi-Fi behind a random key, serving only `manifest.json` and the monthly files already stored there. The QR holds one short address of the same shape the PC script prints (`http://<ip>:8787/<key>/manifest.json`), so there are no data QRs, and the other register scans it with the existing **Scan QR from PC** and `installFromUrl`, which re-matches the history to its own Shopify catalogue. The page shows how many registers have been sent everything, keeps the screen awake while sharing, and sharing stops by itself after 10 minutes, when the app leaves the screen, or on **Stop sharing**. Switched off in practice mode. New: `src/lib/squareShare.ts` (address, key, request routing, progress; pure), `src/lib/squareShareIO.ts` (the server, using the new `react-native-tcp-socket` dependency and `react-native-device-info` for the Wi-Fi address), `tests/squareshare.test.ts` (including a real HTTP round trip). `squareHistoryIO.ts` gains read-only `storedManifest`, `readStoredFile`, `storedFileExists`; `QR` gains a `label`. Help page `orders/square-history` updated, `help.json` rebuilt, iOS local network text updated. **Needs a native rebuild** (`npm install` then `npm run ios:reset`) because of the new native module. Needs two iPads to confirm (device test T51) | your request |
 | 0151 | 2026-10-17 | AI assistant, patch 2 of 10 (your request): **Help ▸ sparkles button ▸ Ask the assistant**, a plain chat with the model set up in Settings ▸ AI assistant (new route `assistant`, `src/screens/Assistant.tsx`, logic in `src/lib/assistantChat.ts`). **No tools yet**, so the model knows nothing about the shop and says so. Short answers by default scaled to the question, a **More detail** button, reply in the language the cashier writes in, and em and en dashes taken out of replies in code. History is kept on the iPad **per staff member** (`assistant.history.v1.<staff id>` through `kv.ts`, never synced, not in backups), newest 200, cleared only by the bin button; only the newest messages that fit the **Context size** go to the model (a quarter kept free for the reply). A **small scrubber** hides email addresses, phone numbers (Australian and `+` numbers), Luhn valid card numbers and keys on everything typed and again on old history at send time, on every endpoint; the cashier's message is stored already scrubbed with a line saying what was hidden. A banner names each failure (not set up, cannot reach, took too long, key rejected, model not found, wrong address, server problem, odd reply) with **Retry** where it can help, **Open model settings** for people who may edit the settings and *ask the owner or a manager* for everyone else, plus a *still working* line after 5 seconds. **Sending is blocked in practice mode.** The Help button shows only to people who may edit the assistant settings (`ASSISTANT_OPEN_TO_ALL` in `assistantChat.ts`, to be flipped by the audit log patch) and never on the sign in screen. Settings can now open straight onto a page (`open`), the navgraph has `page_assistant` and the `help.assistant` spot. Help page `settings/ask-assistant` (new), `settings/assistant` updated, `help.json` and the graph rebuilt. Tests: new `tests/assistantchat.test.ts` (21). Device test T52. Not added: tools, offline search, audit log, role filtering, streaming (later patches in the plan) | your request |
 | 0152 | 2026-10-17 | AI assistant, patch 3 of 10, first half (your request): the **conversation log**, recording only. Every exchange with the model is written on the iPad, never synced and not in backups: who asked (name and role then), the model and whether the address counted as local or remote, the scrubbed question, the reply, the messages sent (by id once the log has them), a checksum of the exact request, what the scrubber hid by category, and failed requests as errors. One file a day in a **hidden app folder** (`Library/Application Support/assistant-log/`, not Documents, so Files.app cannot see it), finished months packed into gzip, a 200 MB cap that **removes the oldest files and writes a purge line** instead of blocking sending (`assistantLog.ts` logic, `assistantLogIO.ts` folder). The key never reaches a line. A log that cannot be written never stops the answer: a red line tells the cashier to tell a manager. Nothing is logged in practice mode. The chat says conversations are logged for the manager. `ask` was split into `prepare` and `runPrepared` so a failed request can be logged. **The viewer, export, clear, the cap setting and opening the chat to everyone are 0153.** Tests: `tests/assistantlog.test.ts`. Device check: `docs/DEVICE_TESTS.md` T53. |
+| 0161 | 2026-10-18 | AI assistant, patch 5, the data gate (plan 3.1), the next item in the plan that is not a tool: **one place that decides what the model may be shown**, in front of every tool result, with the per-category toggles. New `src/lib/assistantGate.ts` (pure). Nine categories: customer details, email addresses, gift card balances, gift card codes, order totals and items, cost prices and profit, stock and other shop data, payment details, keys and passwords. `resolvePolicy` turns the endpoint (Auto, Local or Remote, from 0149) and the toggles into a decision for each: sent, last four characters only, or not sent. The table in 3.1 is the Auto setting, so a local address gets customer details, emails and balances, a remote one gets none of them, codes are never more than the last four, and payment details and keys are never sent. **Settings ▸ AI assistant ▸ What the assistant may see:** a row for each category with **Auto / Always allow / Never allow** and a line saying what that comes to right now, a warning when Always allow sends customer details to a remote address, and the two never-sent rows shown as fixed. Saved with the other assistant settings (per iPad, in Backup & transfer, not synced), cleaned on load and restore. **Enforced in code:** every tool now declares a field map (`gate`) naming each field it can return and its category, or `content` for tools that return only help text (all four so far). `runToolCall` gates the result before it is cut to size, so the model and the log only hold the gated result. A field the map does not name is dropped, counted and reported by name, so a tool cannot leak a field nobody sorted, and a test helper (`assertNoUnknownFields`) fails when one does. With no policy given the remote rules apply. Free text such as order notes is scrubbed under the same rules (an email or phone number only where that category is sent; card numbers and keys always masked). When something is hidden the model is told the kind (*customer details*), never the content, so it says it cannot show it instead of guessing. **History:** each reply records the kinds of data it was built from; when the address becomes remote or a toggle is switched, a reply that used a kind no longer sent is left out of what the model is given, together with its question, though the cashier can still read it. **Log:** what the gate withheld is counted by category on each tool call and on the event (never the items), and the viewer shows it. The scrubber moved to `assistantScrub.ts` (still exported from `assistantChat.ts`). Help page `settings/assistant` updated, `help.json` rebuilt. Tests: `tests/assistantgate.test.ts`. Device test T59. Not in this patch: any tool that returns shop data (patches 6 to 8), so the toggles have nothing to act on yet; the product and inventory lookup in offline mode; the guide tool, the screen and register context tool and the date and time tool | your request |
 | 0160 | 2026-10-18 | AI assistant, patch 4, the offline mode (plan 3.3), a non-tool item taken from the plan: **when the model cannot answer, the chat still searches**. A question that fails (cannot reach the model, took too long, key rejected, model not found, wrong address, server problem, odd reply) or is asked before the model is set up now shows the red bar as before **and** a box headed *Model offline, showing search results*, listing screens (what each is for, and the taps from the Checkout tab) and help pages (tap one to read it, and a screen that is a tab or a page gets the same **Open** button the link tool makes, checked for the role signed in). It is the same two searches the model's tools use, so the role filter applies: a role is never listed a screen or page it cannot use, and a question about one gets the same *could not find anything* as one about something that does not exist. No model is involved, so the list is labelled as matches and not as an answer. Only the question is stored (scrubbed, as always) with a marker where a reply would be; the list is searched again each time the chat is shown, for whoever is signed in then. **The model is never shown a question that only got a list** (it would read a question with no reply, and some chat templates refuse two user messages in a row). The next question tries the model first, and **Retry** replaces the list with the model's answer instead of repeating the question. No list after **More detail**, and none in practice mode. Send now works before the model is set up. New `src/lib/assistantOffline.ts` (pure), history helpers `tidyOffline`, `forModel`, `withoutExchange` in `assistantChat.ts`, a new `offline` kind of log line (`buildOfflineEvent`, `logOffline`) shown in the conversation log with the screens and pages found and why the model was not used. Help page `settings/ask-assistant` updated, `help.json` rebuilt. Tests: `tests/assistantoffline.test.ts`. Device test T58. Not in this patch: product and inventory lookup in offline mode (needs the product tools and the data gate first), the highlight arrows (guide me there), the guide tool, the screen and register context tool, and the current screen as a starting point | your request |
 | 0159 | 2026-10-18 | AI assistant, patch 4, tool 3 of 4 (your request: one tool at a time): **the link tool** (`show_link`). The assistant can now put a **button under its reply** that opens a help page or a screen: *Open Reports*, or the Taking cash page in Help. The model gives a kind (`doc` or `screen`) and an id it got from a search; `resolveLink` in `src/lib/assistantTools.ts` checks it against what the signed in role may see (the same filters the searches use), and a page or screen the role cannot reach gets exactly the same reply as one that does not exist. The button is not part of the reply text: the loop collects it from the tool call (`AssistantTool.link`), saves it on the reply (`ChatEntry.links`, at most 3, no repeats), and `liveLinks` checks every saved button again each time the chat is drawn, so a button a role can no longer reach disappears. Buttons are never sent back to the model. Only tabs and ordinary pages get a button: each screen in `src/lib/assistantScreens.ts` now has a `target` (a tab to switch to or a page to push), and views, windows and the pages that need a cart, an item or a lesson (`NOT_LINKABLE_ROUTES`: Payment, Cart, New item, Edit item, the chat itself, Training run, Practice terminal) have none, so the reply gives their taps in words. A button can never open a web address. The prompt now names the fourth tool and tells the model never to write a link or an id itself. New `tests/assistantlinks.test.ts` (and the tool list test now expects four tools). Device test T57. **Decided without you:** the plan never says what the link tool is, so I took it to mean tappable buttons to help pages and screens, and kept the highlight arrows ("Guide me there") for the guide tool, as in the plan's answer to question 8. Tell me if you meant something else. Not in this patch: the guide tool (the last of the four), the current screen as a starting point, the offline search, and the tool call limit as a Settings field | your request |
 | 0158 | 2026-10-18 | AI assistant, patch 4, tool 2 of 4 (your request: one tool at a time): **the screen tool**, the navgraph search from the plan. The assistant can now **search the app's screens** (`search_screens`) by name or by what they are for, and says how to open each one from the Checkout tab in the app's own words ("Tap More.", "Tap Orders."). `src/lib/assistantScreens.ts` builds the list once from `src/app.navgraph`: tabs, views, pages and windows of the real till, without overlays or practice-only screens. **Roles are worked out by walking the graph once per role**, dropping every transition and screen that role may not use, so a role is only listed where it can really get there. That matters because Settings has no `roles` on the screen itself, only on the way into it; checking the screen alone would have shown it to a cashier. A screen a role cannot reach gets exactly the same reply as one that does not exist, and no summary shown to a cashier names Settings, Staff or a role (a test checks every one). Every searchable screen in `src/app.navgraph` now has a `summary` and `keywords` (documented in `src/app.navschema`), which is what lets a question in different words find it. Search takes whole sentences and needs one matching word, with more matching words ranking higher. The prompt now mentions the third tool and tells the model to give only the taps the tool lists. Also: `resultText` could return more than the size limit when a cut result was full of quotes (each quote is escaped again inside the wrapper); it now trims until it fits. `npm run graph:build` was run, because `src/lib/appNavgraph.generated.ts` had been out of date since 0151 (the Ask the assistant screen was in the graph but not in the copy the app bundles). New `tests/assistantscreens.test.ts`. Device test T56. Not in this patch: the link tool and the guide tool (next two patches), the current screen as a starting point (needs the screen and register context tool), the offline search, and the tool call limit as a Settings field | your request |
